**How to implement.** The Data step of the flow strip, and the Experiments bay's Data files section moved into it (001 §O 'a left flow strip: Items → Setups → Experiments → Data → …, each step reachable directly'; 001 §O 'the Experiments bay's "Data files" section moves into Data'; .spec-md §3.22: a step appears when it works; spec 0046's rule, kept: measured data belong to the Inverse constructor, `ScrollExtentTests.fs`'s `the Main window opens on Add; the Attach data file section belongs to the Inverse window alone`). The step's panels arrive in steps 324-327. Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S9.3. (1) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`: `ConstructorFlowStep` (steps 238, 242) gains `DataFlowStep` after `ExperimentsFlowStep`: `all` lists Items, Setups, Experiments and Data; its `caption` is `Data` and its `flowUiId` `flowDataStep`. `static member stepsOf (mode : ConstructorMode) : ConstructorFlowStep list` answers `all` for `InverseConstructor` and `all` without `DataFlowStep` for `ForwardConstructor`. `ShowFlowStep DataFlowStep` sets `flowStep` alone, the open bay kept, and changes nothing under `ForwardConstructor`. `SwitchConstructorMode ForwardConstructor` (step 186) from `DataFlowStep` also sets `flowStep` to `ExperimentsFlowStep` and `ribbon` to `BayNames.experiments`; every other switch is unchanged. The private `pickDataFile`, `attachDataFileButton` and `dataFileRow` (`TableAndElementRotationView.fs:pickDataFile`, `:attachDataFileButton`, `:dataFileRow`) MOVE to the new view below and are deleted here; `collectionBuilderView` (`TableAndElementRotationView.fs:collectionBuilderView`) loses its `Data files:` section and its mode match, and its doc and the section comment above it say that the data files are the Data step's; `buildDataFilePickerOptions` stays where it is (`DataFilePickerFolderTests` pins it). (2) New `OpticalConstructor.Ui/DataStepView.fs`, `module OpticalConstructor.Ui.DataStepView`, compiled directly after `FlowStripView.fs` (step 242) and before `KitWindowView.fs`: one `<Compile>` line and no comment. Its module doc is one to three lines citing 001 §O and spec 0050 S9.3. It holds the three moved functions, their bodies unchanged but for colours, which they take from the `MaterialsWindowView` buttons the import wizard's view uses (step 309), never a copied helper, and `dataStepView (model : TableAndElementRotationModel) (dispatch : TableAndElementRotationMsg -> unit) : IView`, documented in one to three lines: a `ScrollViewer` scrolling both ways around a vertical `StackPanel` carrying `dataStepPanel`, margin 8, holding the heading `Data files:` and the `StackPanel` named `experimentDataFiles` with one `dataFileRow` per experiment (or the hint `(add experiments in the Experiments step, then attach one data file to each)` when there is none), then one row holding the verb `Split a file by key…` carrying `dataSplitFileButton`, which opens the picker through `pickDataFile` and sends `OpenSplitWizard file` (step 321) on a confirmed pick, and is disabled when `model.kitWrites` is `ControlWithheld` (step 185) as the attach verb is. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitWindowView.fs` (steps 188, 242): `DataFlowStep` shows `DataStepView.dataStepView model dispatch` keyed `data`; `OpticalConstructor.Ui/FlowStripView.fs` (step 242) shows one box per step of `ConstructorFlowStep.stepsOf model.constructorMode`. (4) `OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs`, a group after the flow strip's (step 242) under one comment line citing spec 0050 S9.3, each with a one-line doc: `flowDataStep` (`"FlowDataStep"`), `dataStepPanel` (`"DataStepPanel"`) and `dataSplitFileButton` (`"DataSplitFileButton"`). `OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs`: the doc of `attachDataFile` and `dataFileStatus` names the Data step. No other control, message or option is added. Tests. `KitWindowModelTests` (step 238): `the flow strip's steps follow 001's order and a window opens on Setups` lists Items, Setups, Experiments and Data with their captions, its other assertions kept; new `the Data step is the Inverse constructor's alone, and leaving the Inverse constructor leaves it`: `stepsOf ForwardConstructor` is Items, Setups and Experiments and `stepsOf InverseConstructor` adds Data; over `initInverse`, `ShowFlowStep DataFlowStep` sets `DataFlowStep` with the bay kept, and `SwitchConstructorMode ForwardConstructor` then answers `ExperimentsFlowStep` with `BayNames.experiments`; over `initMain ()` `ShowFlowStep DataFlowStep` changes nothing. `KitWindowTests` (steps 185, 242): `the flow strip UiIds are the stable intent-named ids` also pins `FlowDataStep`, `DataStepPanel` and `DataSplitFileButton`; `the flow strip shows Items, Setups and Experiments left of the surface its step shows` also finds, in the inverse window, the Data box below Experiments and, on `DataFlowStep`, `dataStepPanel` present and `tableElementCanvas` absent, and in the Main window no Data box; `a read-only window withholds every write control` looks for the `attachDataFile` of `E1` and `dataSplitFileButton` in `dataStepView` mounted over the same models (disabled read-only, enabled read-write) and finds no `attachDataFile` in the Experiments bay; with trait `ui-smoke`, new `pressing the Data step shows the data files and the Split a file by key button`: pressing `flowDataStep` in the inverse kit window shows `dataStepPanel`, the `attachDataFile` of E1 and `dataSplitFileButton`. `ScrollExtentTests`: `Inverse: the Experiments bay with its data-file section leaves everything reachable` is renamed `Inverse: the Experiments bay leaves everything reachable`, its assertion kept; `the Main window opens on Add; the Attach data file section belongs to the Inverse window alone` is renamed `the Main window opens on Add; the Attach data file section belongs to the Inverse window's Data step alone`: the forward and the inverse `mainView` texts hold neither `Data files:` nor `Attach data file…`, `dataStepView` over the inverse model with those experiments holds both, and `stepsOf ForwardConstructor` lacks `DataFlowStep`; new `the kit window's Data step leaves everything reachable`: `assertReachable "KitWindowData"` over a `HostWindow` running `kitWindowView` over the inverse model on `DataFlowStep` with `filledExperiments ()`'s experiments. `DataFilePickerFolderTests` and `InverseConstructorTests` pass as written.

**Acceptance.** After the Data step lands, the Inverse constructor's flow strip MUST show Data after Experiments and the Main constructor's none, the Data step MUST hold every experiment's data-file row and the Split a file by key verb, the Experiments bay MUST hold no data-file section, and leaving the Inverse constructor MUST leave the Data step; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `the Data step is the Inverse constructor's alone, and leaving the Inverse constructor leaves it`, the count rising by 1, and the changed `the flow strip's steps follow 001's order and a window opens on Setups`; ui-smoke MUST pass, including `pressing the Data step shows the data files and the Split a file by key button`, the count rising by 1; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `the kit window's Data step leaves everything reachable`, the renamed `Inverse: the Experiments bay leaves everything reachable` and `the Main window opens on Add; the Attach data file section belongs to the Inverse window's Data step alone`, and the changed `the flow strip UiIds are the stable intent-named ids`, `the flow strip shows Items, Setups and Experiments left of the surface its step shows` and `a read-only window withholds every write control`, the count rising by 1; and build, elevation and the sixteen s31 invariants MUST pass.
